    "description": "These maps represent the standard deviation of the classification of five different models, trained on different cross-validation splits. The units are arbitrary. Higher values mean that the models did not agree well in a certain location, which can be a hint to degraded classification performance, high temporal dynamics (logging, dying trees) or to a species mix.",
